evopeg: a build of FFmpeg for the evo framework (https://evoframework.org), configured
down to encoding and muxing audio from standard input to standard output. Nothing of
FFmpeg or of the libraries is changed; the whole recipe is public at
https://github.com/foonerd/evopeg, where each release's notes and the build.json beside
this file name the exact sources, their digests and the configure set.

The binary bin/evopeg is a static link of:

  FFmpeg       GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later
               (ffmpeg-COPYING.LGPLv2.1; ffmpeg-LICENSE.md says which files carry
               other licences). Built without --enable-gpl and without --enable-nonfree:
               no GPL or non-free part of FFmpeg is in it.
  LAME         GNU Library General Public License, version 2 or later
               (lame-COPYING, lame-LICENSE).
  Opus         BSD 3-clause (opus-COPYING).
  libvorbis    BSD 3-clause (vorbis-COPYING).
  libogg       BSD 3-clause (ogg-COPYING).

So the binary as a whole is distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 or later. Its complete corresponding source is the FFmpeg and library
releases named in build.json, obtained from the URLs there, and the recipe in the
evopeg repository, which rebuilds the binary from them. A program that runs evopeg as
a separate process, as the evo framework's plugins do, is not a work based on it.

